{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "medicine-2026",
  "run": 1,
  "simulation_id": "sim-40",
  "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B003",
        "laureates": [
          "Daniel J. Drucker",
          "Jens Juul Holst",
          "Svetlana Mojsov"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of GLP-1 physiology that enabled transformative therapies for diabetes and obesity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B001",
    "B036"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B003 remains the strongest integrated case for a fundamental physiological discovery, a direct and mature therapeutic consequence, and broad established benefit in diabetes and obesity. The proposed citation deliberately limits the achievement to GLP-1 physiology that enabled the therapeutic transformation, rather than assigning the entire subsequent medicinal-development enterprise to three individuals. Within that boundary, Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker remain a coherent allocation across the central physiological, molecular-characterization, and translational understanding contributions.",
    "case_against": "The principal limitation remains that durable therapeutic development involved consequential work not fully represented by this trio, including Lotte Bjerre Knudsen's contribution identified in the discussion. A broad citation about development of all GLP-1 medicines would therefore overstate the allocation. B001 offers a more compact mechanism-to-treatment account, while B036 offers unusually mature preventive impact; both remain serious alternatives.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Thomas Perlmann gives B002 a narrow preference because its three-person allocation may more cleanly delimit the multichannel implant and speech-processing achievement, while questioning whether B003 can fairly contain physiology and therapeutic development within three names.",
        "response": "The attribution advantage of B002 is important, and its durable restoration of speech perception is a major medical achievement. I nevertheless retain B003 because a narrowly physiology-centered citation gives the proposed trio a defensible boundary and captures an unusually direct connection from fundamental physiology to broad, mature treatment across two major metabolic conditions. The remaining B003 credit concern should constrain the citation, not convert it into credit for the whole pharmaceutical-development history."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Sten Linnarsson prioritizes B036 for the durable preventive effect of HPV virus-like-particle vaccines and stresses that its citation must remain distinct from earlier HPV-causation recognition.",
        "response": "I agree that B036 is an exceptional preventive-medicine achievement and that the proposed wording must sharply separate vaccination from HPV causation. That unresolved delimitation, together with the broader pathway of vaccine development, leaves more attribution work on the supplied record. B003 currently provides the more precisely bounded physiology-to-therapy configuration, though B036 remains my leading alternative alongside B001."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Rickard Sandberg supports B003 but emphasizes that the three-person limit excludes substantial later therapeutic-development contributions and requires a distinction between core GLP-1 biology and drug development.",
        "response": "I agree with this distinction. It reinforces my conclusion that the citation should be confined to discoveries of GLP-1 physiology that enabled therapies. On that narrower achievement, Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker remain the most coherent configuration in the supplied discussion; extending the citation to encompass the full development of individual medicines would make the allocation less defensible."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the supplied evidence can further distinguish the individual foundational contributions of Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker from later development of durable therapeutic analogues.",
      "Whether B036's vaccine achievement can be delimited sufficiently from prior HPV-causation recognition and the wider translational pathway.",
      "Whether B002's credited implant and processing advances can be separated sharply enough from later cumulative technical and clinical refinements."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile. The documented Bergen affiliation and shared institutional research settings do not establish a relevant personal connection to any proposed laureate."
  }
}
